        "biography": "Barry Ackroyd\u00a0(born 12 May 1954) is an English\u00a0cinematographer\u00a0and\u00a0director. Ackroyd has frequently worked with directors\u00a0Ken Loach\u00a0and\u00a0Paul Greengrass. He worked on\u00a0Kathryn Bigelow's 2008 war film, The Hurt Locker, and with Greengrass on the critically acclaimed 2013 biographical thriller\u00a0Captain Phillips, the former earning him a\u00a0BAFTA Award\u00a0and an\u00a0Academy Award\u00a0nomination for\u00a0Best Cinematography. In 2014, Ackroyd became the president of the\u00a0British Society of Cinematographers.\n\nDescription above from the Wikipedia article Barry Ackroyd, licensed under CC-BY-SA, full list of contributors on Wikipedia.",
